**Job Description**
**International Sales has an opening for a** 
**Business Development Executive, Specialty to be based in our India office.**
 To support the continued business growth of our Specialty Industries in APAC, we seek a highly motivated and driven individual to be part of the New Business Development team. Reporting to Simon Baker\-Chambers Staff VP, Global Sales, EMEA and APAC, this individual will be responsible to grow the Specialty Industries book including Chemical, Renewables and Forest Products business.




 In this position, the individual will be expected to solicit new business both directly with prospective clients, as well as in collaboration with key broker partners.




**Key Responsibilities**
* Achieve new business objectives as established by the Regional Sales Manager;
* Develop strategy and complete call plans / reports to ensure that all prospects’ information and documentation are updated in SRS (Strategic Relationship System);
* Build and maintain excellent relationships with prospective clients and brokers to successfully create continuous new business opportunities;
* Manage new business opportunities by continuously developing prospects;
* Maintain an active involvement in the local insurance and brokerage community by participating in meetings, conferences and industry\-related functions;
* Maintain a thorough understanding of competitors’ products, services, current pricing strategy and practices.


**Qualifications**
* A Bachelor’s degree in any discipline;
* At least 10 years’ working experience in risk management, loss prevention engineering, claims or underwriting;
* Experience in the broader insurance industry is desired but not essential;
* Knowledge of sales processes (prospecting, nurturing, follow\-up, follow\-through, negotiating, closing) and proven sales experience is a plus;
* Ability to develop strong relationships with clients;
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English
* Excellent interpersonal skills, including facilitating and presentation;
* Excellent planning, organizational and time management skills;
* Technology and social media savvy, including proficiency in Microsoft office software

Full\-Stack Product Engineer

**Tessembl \| Founding Full\-Stack Product Engineer** 




**Location:** 
 \[Mumbai / Hybrid]




**Type:** 
 Full\-time




**Compensation:** 
 Competitive \+ meaningful ESOP




**Apply:** 
 ilhan@tessembl.com



 About Tessembl

 Tessembl is an early stage workforce intelligence company building software that helps organisations make better data informed workforce decisions.




 Our platform will combine workforce data, behavioural insights and analytics within a secure enterprise SaaS environment.




 We are looking for our first engineering hire to help build the product from the ground up.



 The role

 The
 **Founding Full\-Stack Product Engineer** 
 will work directly with the founders and quantitative team to design and build the first commercial versions of Tessembl.




 This is a broad product\-engineering role.




 You will have substantial influence over:



* technical architecture;
* backend systems;
* frontend design;
* database structure;
* APIs;
* cloud infrastructure;
* security;
* engineering standards.


 What you will build

 You will help develop:



* organisation and employee data structures;
* secure enterprise dashboards;
* workforce analytics interfaces;
* assessment workflows;
* reporting and benchmarking tools;
* decision support interfaces;
* data import systems;
* customer administration;
* authentication and access controls;
* analytics and visualisation components.


 Core responsibilities
 * Design and build the initial SaaS architecture.
* Develop frontend and backend systems.
* Design relational data models.
* Build secure multi tenant infrastructure.
* Develop APIs and data\-ingestion pipelines.
* Build analytics\-heavy user interfaces.
* Integrate statistical and machine learning outputs into the product.
* Implement authentication, permissions and role based access.
* Establish audit logging and data quality controls.
* Support cloud deployment, monitoring and backups.
* Integrate with external enterprise systems where required.
* Establish testing, documentation and engineering standards.
* Work directly with early customers during implementation.


 What we are looking for
 * Strong full stack development capability.
* Experience building modern web applications and APIs.
* Strong understanding of databases and data modelling.
* Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure or GCP.
* Understanding of authentication, permissions and SaaS security.
* Ability to work independently in an early\-stage environment.
* Strong product judgement.
* Ability to collaborate closely with data scientists and quantitative teams.


 Likely technology environment

 The final stack will be shaped with the founding engineer, but may include:



* Python;
* TypeScript / JavaScript;
* React or similar modern frontend framework;
* PostgreSQL or similar relational database;
* REST and/or GraphQL;
* Docker;
* AWS / Azure / GCP;
* GitHub;
* modern CI/CD and monitoring tools.


 Particularly valuable experience

 Useful experience includes:



* B2B SaaS;
* enterprise software;
* analytics platforms;
* HR tech;
* data heavy applications;
* dashboards and visualisation;
* ML/data science production systems;
* enterprise integrations;
* secure multi\-tenant architecture.


 Why join

 You will be the first engineering hire and will have meaningful influence over:



* product architecture;
* technology choices;
* engineering culture;
* infrastructure;
* security;
* future technical hiring.



 This role is suited to someone who wants the ownership and influence of an early founding engineer position.

**Your role, your impact**
 As a .NET/BI Analytics Developer, you’ll play a critical role in supporting and enhancing analytics\-driven applications used within the nuclear and financial industries. As part of Alithya’s Digital Applications Data Analytics team, you’ll contribute to the stability, scalability, and continuous improvement of analytics solutions. Your work will directly influence business insights, operational efficiency, and data\-driven decision making.








**Your day\-to\-day**
* Support, maintain, and enhance analytics solutions using .NET, C\#, and Microsoft SQL BI stack;
* Analyze and translate client requirements into technical solutions;
* Develop and manage ETL processes using SSIS and support SSAS\-based data models;
* Design, develop, and optimize SQL queries and database performance;
* Build and maintain applications across front\-end (Angular), middle tier, and back\-end layers;
* Connect and integrate applications with various data sources, including SQL, NoSQL, and Big Data platforms;
* Perform debugging, testing, and deployment using Visual Studio or VS Code;
* Collaborate with cross\-functional teams to deliver high\-quality solutions;
* Support ongoing improvements, issue resolution, and system enhancements;
* Work on Azure cloud services, ensuring scalability, performance, and high availability;
* Contribute to DevOps practices, including CI/CD and infrastructure automation.






**Keys to your success**
* Bachelor’s degree in computer science, software engineering, or a related field;
* Minimum 5 years of experience in .NET and/or BI development roles;
* Experience with Microsoft SQL BI stack, including SSIS and SSAS;
* Experience working with Azure cloud services and deployment strategies;
* Strong proficiency in SQL and database performance optimization;
* Hands\-on experience with C\# and Angular\-based web applications;
* Strong understanding of data modelling, reporting, and analytics solutions;
* Familiarity with DevOps practices and automation tools;
* Demonstrated commitment to continuous learning and professional growth.


**Language Skills**
* English: Proficient






**Our mission, your future**
 As a global network of trusted advisors, we create cutting\-edge technological solutions to overcome today’s challenges and anticipate tomorrow’s needs. It all starts with the collaboration of a diverse team of passionate innovators, each driven to make a difference. Together, we challenge the status quo and push each other to new heights.




 Ready to leave your mark on engaging mandates and shape the future through digital transformation and strategic consulting? Take your ambitions to the next level and discover your next exciting challenge with us!








**Our commitments**
* Our authenticity is our strength: The diversity of our backgrounds, experiences, thoughts and insights is our competitive advantage. We foster a collaborative environment where we embrace our authenticity and leverage our unique perspectives to collectively build the future we all envision.
